{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 0d7d986178a44c38d4c92d35b2112226cc16544e. I reviewed the design/report and all 20 artifacts, including dependency-lock metadata, pinned vendor provenance, source, tests and dated results. Three P2 findings:\n\n1. Preserve unresolved sends after ordinary transport failures, not just process crashes (src/agent.ts #act, lines 215-238; pi-durable tool settlement). The prepared envelope lives only in the tool task's memo. If Room admission succeeds but replies are lost through all four client attempts, replay() throws, pi-durable terminalizes the failed tool and removes its memo, and the conversation ends without its receipt. Retrying the same requestId returns that completed error instead of recovering the act. My workerd probe wraps the actual RpcWire.submit: it first calls the real Room, then drops every propose reply with retryable unavailable/maybeRecorded:true. Exactly one propose is in the Room log, four sends occurred, the lane document holds only claim, and the subsequent same-request retry returns the old error even after the wire is restored. Store unresolved signed envelopes in durable state that outlives tool settlement, or keep a durable recovery task pending until the original receipt or a definite refusal is obtained; never sign a replacement to clear an unknown outcome. Add this failure case and reconciliation across reset to the spike, and qualify the current recovery claim.\n\n2. Save the commit identity before pushing it (src/agent.ts artroom_write, lines 286-290). The tool creates/pushes a new commit through controls.workspace before memoizing its head. The existing write:after-push injection actually occurs after that memo is saved, leaving the external-effect/local-record gap untested. My additional workerd probe uses the unchanged tool, pushes through the existing real-object fake, then aborts its Agent from the workspace callback before it returns. Recovery pushes a second, different SHA and lands that second head. This does not duplicate a signed claim/propose/land, but disproves the replay-safe push rule in Q7 and the comment that a rerun reuses the first pushed head. Separate preparation from publication, durably save the exact commit and expected ref before the first push, and on an uncertain result reconcile/re-push that same commit. Test resets both before and after recording the external outcome. Keep the explicit simulated-push and untested workspace-token boundaries.\n\n3. Make the standalone type-check fail when the compiler cannot run (scripts/check.sh; package.json/lockfile). No TypeScript dependency is installed by the documented spike-only npm ci, and neither compiler path exists in a fresh checkout. The script captures and discards the command failure, searches only for 'error TS', and exits 0 with 'spike sources: no type errors'. It still reports success after adding const checkerImpossible: number = \"definitely a type error\". Pin/provide the compiler, fail missing tools and compiler/configuration errors, and limit any vendor-error exception to the deliberately enumerated vendor diagnostics. An actual installed TypeScript compiler detects that deliberate error. After removing it, the exact spike has no own-file diagnostics but 17 vendor diagnostics; that is a scoped check, not a clean whole-program check.\n\nArchitecture: the small queued SQLite facade matches the pinned portable database contract; rollback and storage conformance run in a real Durable Object. The stored-envelope rule works at the nine tested signed-act crash boundaries. Authority remains in Room; no protocol amendment is needed for this spike. Production still needs the alarm loop, attention bridge, durable unresolved-send handling, lease renewal/release and abort behavior, and current Room/client integration tests. Q5 also needs an explicit context handoff between separate identity Durable Objects: pi-durable fork is within one harness/storage, so an author's native fork does not automatically exist in a separately keyed reviewer's object.\n\nSecurity: the Room judged the real delegated acts; simulated pushes bypass workspace tokens and do not prove their handling. Test-only public setup/run/transcript/usage RPC and a JWK in SQLite are accurately bounded to the spike; production must enforce caller/viewer/steerer identity and secret custody before exposing these operations. Recovering old receipts after delegation/key revocation over a binding is correctly identified as a client gap and must remain tracked. Independent reviewer credentials, expired/compromised delegation, refusals, lease fencing, cancellation during unknown sends and token exclusion require adversarial tests. Do not treat a model's final answer as proof of landing: the saved live transcript says landed while its tool reported accepted; the external test alarm later proves landed.\n\nSimplification: retain one Room authority and one conversation per lane; use Room updates for outcomes and harness state for orchestration. No second approval/admission system is needed. Keep the complete section-7 scope; day estimates are sequencing information only and cannot narrow functionality. Turn untested pieces into gitseq implementation requests before the spike becomes a product integration.\n\nValidation: fresh isolated checkout; spike-only npm ci --ignore-scripts; pinned git-archive setup; 39 scripted tests passed and 1 live test skipped with provider-key/model environment variables unset. Two additional real-workerd diagnostics passed (push/memo crash; admitted act with all replies lost). The missing-compiler/type-error probe reproduces the false success. Actual compiler verification gives no spike-owned errors, with the vendor exceptions above. Recorded live result inspected; no model API call or deployment performed. Pinned upstream README/spec/tool/database contract checked against official source and installed 1.0.0. Saved diagnostic fixtures: /tmp/artroom-checker-pi-durable-diagnostics/{checker-push-window.test.ts,checker-unknown-outcome.test.ts,checker-missing-compiler.ts}; copy test fixtures back to their original test path in the isolated checkout to run them. All temporary edits removed; checkout clean.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:75a785bad5c1458bc12f0a9c41eabef601499f54","binding":"assigned","head":"0d7d986178a44c38d4c92d35b2112226cc16544e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3ea010b518b1c9cf97e6ec29509caac265e86a80\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:217f6833e24f7747c35877bf206380c1bb56f526\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4f82b35e42b508a12b2f3ff9ae6a363f8c24c744","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}